module tasks.`2026-11-22-python-card-status-shapes`

task PythonCardStatusShapes {
  title "Python cards render without status for cancelled and moved-to-background python_execute replies; make the real-session smoke hermetic"
  verify $ cargo nextest run -p bboxy450-harness --features acp-agent,embedded --lib -E 'test(python_cell) | test(real_session_smoke) | test(codex_outcome)'
  paths "crates/bboxy450-harness"
  brief """
    Our stand: one parser per shape; fixtures, not live data, decide a gate.

    ## Evidence (Oracle, 2026-11-22)
    `make test-real-sessions` fails on main `42dac19c3` and on `fe4a3723d`: `SMOKE BAD ~/.bboxy450-harness/sessions/01M7VC8QBWY7P55AVTX648HXKJ.jsonl: python without status: mcp__bboxy__python_execute` (x2), `crates/bboxy450-harness/src/frontends/face_core.rs:1438` "2 cards render wrong". That file is the Oracle seat's own session; its two odd python_execute replies are a run the Oracle cancelled (`python_execution_cancel` while running) and a run the client moved to the background ("moved to the background as task ... it keeps running") that later failed. Log: `~/mydev/bbx-gate-repairs/target/fixture-handoff/watcher-fix/registered-coverage/baseline-real-sessions.log`.

    ## Do
    1. Extract the two reply shapes from that session (redacted, minimal) into fixtures beside `face_core.rs` tests; teach `python_cell` to give them a status (`cancelled`; `running`/handle-only -> `running` until a later `python_execution_get` resolves it), reusing the existing status mapping.
    2. Make the gate hermetic: `test-real-sessions` stays an opt-in smoke over live logs, but the fixtures, not live data, decide CI; the real-session smoke must not be part of `make test-parity`'s pass/fail unless pointed at a fixture directory.
    Land through harness main, `make bump-harness`, `make land`. Long commands detached.
    ## Oracle amendment, 2026-11-22 03:10
    - Granted `scripts/ci-local.sh` (it calls `test-real-sessions` unconditionally at `:117`) and `Cargo.lock` for the harness bump. Keep `make test-real-sessions` as the opt-in live-log smoke; CI calls it only with an explicit `SESSIONS_DIR` (the fixture directory). Shapes confirmed by the executor: a missing-result placeholder after cancellation, and a client text notice for a background task.


    ## Report from seat:01M7ZVK9YFPRSBR7EJF6DPC5E1

    Landed Python card statuses and fixture-only default CI at signed term 8213133a75e83ee6b0c445a54b4219c036096bd0, pinned to signed harness bd8a855d6bac17b578de0b93d951ea08f31e69e0. The requested Nextest command exited 0 with 6 tests. Explicit test-real-sessions passed 2 tests and replayed one fixture file with two cards and no errors. Both make land commands exited 0 and standalone native/TLC parity matched 531 models. Removed unconditional session replay, ambient replay input, and the duplicate missing-result literal. The follow-up uses a typed string view for both embedded and published image assets.

